{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus","id":791143,"title":"Worldwide Wolf Population and Tribal Lupus","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-22T16:24:04-08:00","id":791143,"title":"Worldwide Wolf Population and Tribal Lupus","content":"I recently looked at the worldwide wolf population. I think we can figure out some basics of the lupus population in each tribe as a result. Worldwide wolf population is between 200,000 to 400,000. Numbers are only approximate as the data is inconsistent even in the same articles I read. The totals below support the lower limit of 200,000, but uncertainty certainly makes it possible for lots of unknown wolf stock that the Garou may be kept hidden. However, the overall ratios from region to region likely remain the same.<br /> <br /> General breakdown is:<br /> <br /> North America (78,000 total)<br /> Canada - 60,000<br /> Alaska - 12,000<br /> Rockies - 2000<br /> Great Lakes - 4000<br /> Other (Greenland, US Southwest) - 100<br /> <br /> Europe (15,000 total)<br /> Scandinavia (incl Finland) - 400<br /> Spain &amp; Portugal - 2000<br /> Italy - 700<br /> Balkans - 6000<br /> Central Europe - 1200<br /> Belarus - 2000<br /> Ukraine - 2000<br /> Baltic - 1200<br /> <br /> Asia (90,000 total)<br /> Russia (including European Russia) - 30,000<br /> Turkey - 7000<br /> Central Asia - 40,000<br /> Mongolia - 10,000<br /> India - 1000<br /> China - 1000<br /> Middle East - 1000<br /> <br /> Africa (unknown, but populations include Egypt and Ethiopia)<br /> <br /> If we assume jackals are also possible to be kinfolk for Silent Striders and Bone Gnawers at least, then there are several hundred thousand of them as well.<br /> <br /> We can see the big areas for wolf population is northern North America (Canada and Alaska plus bits of northern US) and the Eurasian steppe and taiga (Russia, Central Asia, and Mongolia). That is 78,000 plus 80,000. Eastern Europe adds another 12,000. All the lupus will be concentrated there. What does this tell us based on known tribal populations?<br /> <br /> <b>Red Talons</b>, of course, are the tribe with the most lupus. Every member is one except for a few metis. Talons would mainly be limited to Russia and northern North America. Their vestigal populations in Europe (particularly western Europe) and southern Asia were probably lost long ago, although there could be a few septs here and there with one or two packs.<br /> <br /> <b>Wendigo</b> would be a tribe with lots of lupus. Perhaps the only tribe whose lupus population is around the same level of homids since Wendigo human kinfolk are also few in number. That the Wendigo may be the only tribe that is around 50/50 would be a good distinction for the tribe. It should probably be emphasized more.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Fangs</b> and <b>Shadow Lord</b>s would also have relatively larger amount of lupus than the average for the Garou. Their tribal homelands in Eurasia sit right on top one of the last few large populations of wolves. Probably not 50%, but they should have significantly more than 10%. Perhaps a 20-30% range. Let's give the Silver Fangs more than the Shadow Lords as proper for the eldest tribe of kings, so Silver Fangs more around 30% and Shadow Lords 20%.<br /> <br /> Those are the obvious choices. We now need to start making some assumptions.<br /> <br /> <b>Stargazers</b> may have more than the usual number of lupus. Their tribal homeland doesn't have many interlopers and they are right in the middle of China. India, and Central Asia. Given their small numbers canonically, a significant percentage may be lupus. Somewhere between 20-50%.<br /> <br /> Based on Geography, we can see both the <b>Get of Fenris</b> and <b>Black Furies</b> operate in European areas where there are wolves (stories of Amazons happen in Turkey and Central Asia, and the Germanic migrations once had many Germanic tribes in eastern Europe (Poland, Ukraine, Kievan Rus) as well as their current range in Scandinavia and Baltic). They are probably in the 10-20% range. They have lots of competitors though.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Gaia</b> likely have a decent number of lupus with the main stock being in the Middle East, but with a few populations retained here and there elsewhere. Let's give them the canonical average of 10%.<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Striders</b> are in a bind. North Africa has almost no wolves. They may have access to some packs in the Middle East, India, and Balkans but are fighting for them against the Children, Silver Fangs, Black Furies, and a few others. Let's say they are near the overall average between 5-10%.<br /> <br /> That leaves the other tribes at lower than average. Naturally this would include the urban tribes of <b>Glass Walkers</b> and <b>Bone Gnawers</b>. They probably have close to 0%. Population may be in the dozens or fewer. Glass Walkers may have a special kennel breeding program trying to maintain the last few wolves of their tribal bloodline. The source is likely Italy where the Glass Walkers have had a long association since the time of Rome. Bone Gnawer lupus likely originate from India.<br /> <br /> What might be a surprise are the other two big losers - the <b>Uktena</b> and <b>Fianna</b>. Their traditional geographic homelands have almost no wolves. The Uktena may have access to a few wolves as charity from the Younger Brother Wendigo, but the Fianna are screwed unless they control wolf stock in the Iberian population from the days when the Celtic tribes ruled there. And they probably have lots of competition there. Interesting to speculate that if you are a lupus Fianna, your default &quot;culture&quot; is Spanish, not Celtic. For these tribes, lupus stock is probably between 0-5%.<br /> <br /> Of course, tribes are not strictly limited to the most natural territories. Moon bridges and immigration send tribes all over the world. We can determine that Canada (and northern US) likely is prime ground for the Tribes to fight over control of wolf kinfolk. I can see lots of tribes that don't have many (or any) wolves in their traditional homelands, emigrating to Canada and fighting for control of wolf stock. In fact, for some tribes (like the Fianna), this is probably the ONLY origin of wolf kinfolk. The whole country is probably in a prolonged struggle with Red Talons and Wendigo fighting Get of Fenris and Fianna as their main rivals, with the other tribes as interlopers. Maybe even the Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers snatch a few lupus here and there. Given the prominence of Silver Fang wolf kin in Eurasia, I imagine the Silver Fangs mostly stay out of this fight let. They may have a few traditional wolf packs in these lands though that they brought over from Eurasia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T20:30:55-08:00","id":792922,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the population of wolves be larger in the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> People are more concentrated in cities, which leaves more wilderness habitat in between by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T21:05:58-08:00","id":792931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus?p=792922#post792922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the population of wolves be larger in the World of Darkness?<br /> <br /> People are more concentrated in cities, which leaves more wilderness habitat in between by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, secret Hakken wolfpacks in Japan.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T11:05:40-08:00","id":793200,"title":"","content":"As I said, there is room for more unknown wolf stock the Garou keep hidden, but the overall population ratio for various reasons likely stay the same.<br /> <br /> The idea is to draw some conclusions from real world populations and see how that impacts the tribes. Personally, I think it is interesting to consider that the Wendigo may be the only tribe with near 50/50 split, and that the Fianna may be one of the more wolf starved tribes. If you want Ireland to be populated with lots of wolves kept secret from humans in your chronicles, go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T13:27:13-08:00","id":793247,"title":"","content":"For Silent Striders it is interesting to note the African Red Jackal was proved to be a Wolf species this year.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Ethiopian_wolf_%28Canis_simensis_citernii%29.jpg/1280px-Ethiopian_wolf_%28Canis_simensis_citernii%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> Ethiopian wolf - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopian_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopian_wolf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It possible in the WoD the Striders always knew the truth and have Lupus from this population.<br /> <br /> Tiny population and in danger of going extinct, but a viable breeding stock for lupus Silent Striders nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T17:14:06-08:00","id":793323,"title":"","content":"The Striders were always unusual as their Pure Breed showed they really hail from jackal stock and not wolf. Therefore, I always thought of them as werejackals who were nevertheless Garou. The less pure breed Striders have more wolf blood in them. It's less strange than marsupials being werewolves. If the Silent Striders were originally werejackals who crossed over into actual wolves, I also think the Bone Gnawers were werewolves who crossed over into jackals in some of their areas (India, Middle East, and North Africa) because the jackals were scavengers like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:01:52-08:00","id":793349,"title":"","content":"The ethiopian wolf should also be viable Garou stock in Africa, though their range is fairly small, especially now. I'm not sure what their historical range has been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T18:17:13-08:00","id":793355,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/0/0a/Walks_with_Might_lupus.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130721004939\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <img src=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/4/4d/Walks_with_Might_Crinos.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20130721005029\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Always thought he looked like an Ethiopian wolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T21:22:50-08:00","id":793409,"title":"","content":"The Ethiopian Wolf seems to have been limited to the Ethiopian highlands and was always a relatively low population. If they were breeding stock for any tribe, it makes most sense to be Silent Striders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T11:47:38-08:00","id":794296,"title":"","content":"Wolves in New Brunswick Canada: 0<br /> Eastern Coyote: A large species of Coyote due to interbreeding with Wolves long ago. Lots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T18:43:10-08:00","id":795285,"title":"","content":"The large numbers of coyote-wolf hybrids out there poses the question of whether they could be the basis for animal breed Nuwisha, Garou, both, or neither. Canine crossbreeding calls a lot into question.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for the fact that Nuwisha only have one auspice, I'd simply make them part of the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T20:08:24-08:00","id":795330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus?p=795285#post795285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The large numbers of coyote-wolf hybrids out there poses the question of whether they could be the basis for animal breed Nuwisha, Garou, both, or neither. Canine crossbreeding calls a lot into question.<br /> <br /> If it wasn't for the fact that Nuwisha only have one auspice, I'd simply make them part of the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an interesting idea, bringing the Nuwisha into the fold. If they were always a part of Garou society since prehistory, I don't think it would be difficult to make them all play the role of the Ragabash.<br /> If they are being integrated at a later date, that could pose some problems. I can only imagine the proud werewolves would chafe at being 'taught' by those they view as outsiders, outsiders who can be very vicious jokers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T09:07:29-08:00","id":796858,"title":"","content":"It is worth bearing in mind that five generations without infusion of fresh Garou blood will breed out the Kin - and that Garou are only a little more fertile than humans, and not as fertile as wolves - and that only 6 or so Red Talons are born a year according to their revised tribebook. What this suggests is that while there are many wolves, there is very little breeding going on with them as a result, and there will accordingly actually be very few wolf kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-30T15:23:14-08:00","id":797041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus?p=795330#post795330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an interesting idea, bringing the Nuwisha into the fold. If they were always a part of Garou society since prehistory, I don't think it would be difficult to make them all play the role of the Ragabash.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Nuwisha should have been very close to the three Pure Ones tribes from an early start. But even if they considered them to be their Little Nephews or whatever, I think it would be hard for the Eurasian Garou to accept them (like they obviously accepted the werejackals of the Silent Striders) because they just don't have the five auspices.<br /> <br /> Still, they inexplicably accepted weremarsupials as Garou which never made sense to me despite the tortured explanation of why the Bunyip were actually Garou as opposed to a different Changing Breed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T05:36:48-08:00","id":811072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_golden_wolf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/42/African_wolf%2C_Dagana%2C_Senegal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_golden_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> African wolf - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_golden_wolf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_golden_wolf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Jackals&quot; of North Africa are not actually jackals at all, even though they can interbreed with them. And even though they aren't wolves, they are more closely related to them than jackals, so the Garou of Northern Africa can easily have lots of Lupus in their ranks, just little strange looking though. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:58:16-08:00","id":811488,"title":"","content":"If we count the various jackal breeds that have lots of wolf genetics, it certainly would boost the lupus population of certain tribes. Probably Silent Striders, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Glass Walkers in that order. That shouldn't impact how many lupus of the tribe are seen in most chronicles (since they are usually placed in North America or Europe), but it would provide a nice contrast of those tribes in those lands and if the PCs ever visit the &quot;homeland&quot; in North Africa and Middle East where the lupus population actually exists. It also means should lupus characters of those tribes show up, they should reflect the populace of the MENA region when they go in homid form.<br /> <br /> I think the jackal population is one of those areas where the ST has to do more thinking about his chronicle as it impacts some things. It's only strange that for the Silent Striders, it is more likely that the more jackal they are, they higher pure breed they are; but for any other tribe it's likely a sign of low or zero Pure Breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T03:17:06-08:00","id":811642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus?p=811488#post811488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we count the various jackal breeds that have lots of wolf genetics, it certainly would boost the lupus population of certain tribes. Probably Silent Striders, Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Glass Walkers in that order. That shouldn't impact how many lupus of the tribe are seen in most chronicles (since they are usually placed in North America or Europe), but it would provide a nice contrast of those tribes in those lands and if the PCs ever visit the &quot;homeland&quot; in North Africa and Middle East where the lupus population actually exists. It also means should lupus characters of those tribes show up, they should reflect the populace of the MENA region when they go in homid form.<br /> <br /> I think the jackal population is one of those areas where the ST has to do more thinking about his chronicle as it impacts some things. It's only strange that for the Silent Striders, it is more likely that the more jackal they are, they higher pure breed they are; but for any other tribe it's likely a sign of low or zero Pure Breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was, North Africa doesn't have jackals. African golden wolves may resemble them, but are not the same species. But yeah, good point about the tribes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The chronicle I'm starting has Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers as main tribes so I can easily use Northern African tribe members as visitors, or can set adventure in North Africa. Lean Garou with yellow coats with white stomach, throat and face markings and yellow eyes, not the most usual sight for Polish werewolves. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:25:47-08:00","id":812258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus?p=811642#post811642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was, North Africa doesn't have jackals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You bring up a great point, and I'd like to discuss it in more depth.<br /> <br /> According to genetic evidence in 2015, they are closer to grey wolves than they are to the golden jackals. But for the previous six thousand years, people called them jackals. And it is not simply the case that they are true wolves (canis lupus) - they aren't. If we are going by mitochondrial evidence, coyotes are closer to grey wolves than the African golden wolf - but we don't call them wolves. If the African golden wolf is truly a wolf - then so are coyotes.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.theguardian.com/science/grrlscientist/2015/jul/30/golden-jackal-a-new-wolf-species-hiding-in-plain-sight\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> link has some in depth information.<br /> <br /> It does cement the idea that Silent Striders, despite looking much like jackals in their purest breed forms, are still werewolves specifically and not were-canines in general. Calling them &quot;wolf&quot; instead of &quot;jackal&quot; means we are slotting them closer to the species they share the most genetic commonality with, but they still are not canis lupus. They are farther away than coyotes are. We use terms like wolves and jackals because those are the words we already have, but it would probably be best if we had a different word for them (and the Ethiopian Wolf) like we do for coyotes. The Ethiopian Wolf has been renamed many, many times by scientists trying to get it right. But they are not canis lupus or a sub-species, they are a distant relation to canis lupus.<br /> <br /> We are getting into the semantics area here on what should be &quot;properly&quot; called wolf. If it is not strictly the grey wolf, but to another ancestor, we are expanding what animals should be considered wolves. Where should we stop?<br /> <br /> All members of the canis genus - grey wolves, coyotes, golden jackals, dingoes, dogs - can all produce fertile offspring when mating. Should all of them be considered &quot;wolves&quot; for the purpose of the &quot;True&quot; jackals like the black back and side striped jackal don't seem to be able to produce fertile offspring with other members of canis, but in theory they could. Golden jackals (and I mean them, not golden wolves) can also breed with other members of canis though.<br /> <br /> The Kucha Ekundu are &quot;Red Talons&quot; that are African Wild Dogs which are close to most canis, but is genetically different (but with the same number of chromosomes) and so far we haven't seen any hybrids with them. If they are considered wolves, then we are entering a world where the rules are very loose and fast. We are almost getting into Bunyip territory here!<br /> <br /> How far should one base the definition of wolf, jackal, or coyotes on science versus myth. It's an appropriate question in the World of Darkness. We are left with several choices. One is that Nuwisha ARE actually Garou (since the more distant African golden wolves are), but that Coyote lead them astray so that Luna can't bestow any auspice on them other than Ragabash. The second is that jackal like Silent Striders aren't Garou (since the closer coyotes aren't either), but were &quot;adopted&quot; into the Garou Nation. They aren't wolves, nor are they true jackals - but something inbetween. A third option is that this isn't based on science at all, but ancient myth and legend and the spirits who have their own version of truth different than technocratic science. In that option, the african jackal/wolves are Garou, and the coyotes aren't, simply because that is what the spirits and Gaia wanted.<br /> <br /> None are intrinsically correct or wrong, but choosing one over the others will have implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T00:29:26-08:00","id":812424,"title":"","content":"Thanks, hadn't thought about coyotes! It would seem I simply have to make a choice, and that Fera &quot;genetics&quot; are really messy business (just like real world ones) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll propably use the option where Nuwisha are Garou but their totem has done his tricks succesfully, and they can only become Ragabash. This has been very useful discussion, gave lot to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:27:14-08:00","id":813065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazy_Ivan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/791143-worldwide-wolf-population-and-tribal-lupus?p=812424#post812424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll propably use the option where Nuwisha are Garou but their totem has done his tricks succesfully, and they can only become Ragabash.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is a viable choice, and has all sorts of interesting things that can come out in play.<br /> <br /> Did the Croatan, Wendigo, and Uktena see the Nuwisha as one of them, but led astray? Do they call them brother, cousin, sister?<br /> <br /> If so, did the Old World Garou accept that viewpoint, or did they reject it? Or is it a controversy within the nation?<br /> <br /> How do people see Coyote as a spirit/totem? Are they outraged he violated the decisions of Luna? Are they amazed at his power to do so? Do they think Luna and Gaia were fine with this and it has some hidden plan? Probably there is split reaction of all viewpoints (including that Nuwisha aren't really Garou). Having pulled such a feat means Coyote is a bit more than just an annoying trickster, which is probably how it should be.<br /> <br /> Also, all sorts of stories to why Coyote did that. Was it just because he could, or is there some purpose? Was it a selfish or heroic act?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}